# Verbs in -ся in Russian: учу́сь, занима́юсь
subtitle: "Meet the little ся on Russian verbs: я учу́сь, фильм начина́ется, как э́то называ́ется? — and when it is сь instead."
tags: ["russian","reflexive verbs","учиться","russian grammar","russian verbs"]
teaches: ["grammar/reflexive-verbs"]
thumb: "band \"The little ся that means myself\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Going in Russian: иду or хожу?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/62-russian-idti-hodit.cast"}

## Verbs in -ся in Russian: учу́сь, занима́юсь
